  "code": "GLUCN",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Parameter</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal Range</strong> (fasting, adults)*</th>\n<th><strong>Increased Glucagon</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Decreased Glucagon</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Glucagon</strong></td>\n<td><strong>50 &ndash; 150 pg/mL</strong> (varies by lab)</td>\n<td>- <strong>Glucagonoma</strong> (rare pancreatic &alpha;-cell tumor; associated with diabetes, weight loss, necrolytic migratory erythema) - Uncontrolled <strong>diabetes mellitus</strong> - Severe stress, sepsis, trauma, burns - Acute pancreatitis - Cushing&rsquo;s syndrome</td>\n<td>- Chronic pancreatitis (&alpha;-cell loss) - Pancreatic cancer (non-&alpha; cell destruction) - Cystic fibrosis (pancreatic insufficiency) - Post-pancreatectomy state - Rare congenital &alpha;-cell dysfunction</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"914\" data-end=\"1055\">\n<p data-start=\"916\" data-end=\"1055\"><strong data-start=\"916\" data-end=\"928\">Glucagon</strong> is a hormone secreted by pancreatic <strong data-start=\"965\" data-end=\"976\">&alpha;-cells</strong> that raises blood glucose by stimulating glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1056\" data-end=\"1266\">\n<p data-start=\"1058\" data-end=\"1130\">The test is <strong data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1104\">not commonly ordered routinely</strong>; it is usually used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1133\" data-end=\"1266\">\n<li data-start=\"1133\" data-end=\"1173\">\n<p data-start=\"1135\" data-end=\"1173\">Diagnose or monitor <strong data-start=\"1155\" data-end=\"1170\">glucagonoma</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1176\" data-end=\"1218\">\n<p data-start=\"1178\" data-end=\"1218\">Evaluate <strong data-start=\"1187\" data-end=\"1215\">unexplained hypoglycemia</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1221\" data-end=\"1266\">\n<p data-start=\"1223\" data-end=\"1266\">Assess <strong data-start=\"1230\" data-end=\"1263\">pancreatic endocrine function</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1267\" data-end=\"1427\">\n<p data-start=\"1269\" data-end=\"1427\">Interpretation should always be correlated with <strong data-start=\"1317\" data-end=\"1425\">clinical findings, glucose levels, and other pancreatic hormone assays (insulin, C-peptide, proinsulin).</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
